From: Alexis Belmonte <alexbelm48@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Disable Lumen surface cache feedback on Linux

Recent Linux GPU drivers (notably the NVIDIA open kernel module 610.x on Blackwell)
fault with VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST while submitting the Lumen surface cache feedback
GPU readback. The failure is reported later at the next fence wait because the
error is sticky. Disabling the feedback readback on Linux avoids the device loss;
it only affects Lumen surface-cache resolution adaptation, not core rendering.

Scoped to LinuxEngine.ini so Windows/Mac cross-compiled targets are unaffected.
---
 Engine/Config/Linux/LinuxEngine.ini | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/Config/Linux/LinuxEngine.ini b/Engine/Config/Linux/LinuxEngine.ini
--- a/Engine/Config/Linux/LinuxEngine.ini
+++ b/Engine/Config/Linux/LinuxEngine.ini
@@ -8,6 +8,11 @@
 ;Perplatform to PerQualityLevel conversion mapping for platform groups
 QualityLevelMapping="high"
 r.Shadow.DetectVertexShaderLayerAtRuntime=1
+; Recent Linux drivers (NVIDIA open kernel 610.x / Blackwell) fault with
+; VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST while submitting the Lumen surface cache feedback GPU
+; readback; disable the feedback readback on Linux to avoid the device loss.
+r.LumenScene.SurfaceCache.Feedback=0
+r.Lumen.Reflections.SurfaceCacheFeedback=0

 [TextureStreaming]
 ; PoolSizeVRAMPercentage is how much percentage of GPU Dedicated VRAM should be used as a TexturePool cache for streaming textures (0 - unlimited streaming)
